+### `mcp_manager_add`
+
+Add an MCP server, or replace the entry with the same name. The harness mounts it immediately and its tools become callable as `mcp__<name>__<tool>`. For the stdio transport give command/args/env/cwd; for streamable-http give url/headers. Env values and headers carry credentials; prefer referencing a secret over pasting it.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "name": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Stable local namespace for this server (the model sees its tools as mcp__<name>__<tool>). Use [A-Za-z0-9_-], 1-32 characters; unique among configured servers."
+    },
+    "transport": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "stdio spawns a local program; streamable-http connects to a service.",
+      "enum": [
+        "stdio",
+        "streamable-http"
+      ]
+    },
+    "enabled": {
+      "type": "boolean",
+      "description": "Whether to mount the server now; defaults to true."
+    },
+    "command": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "stdio: executable to spawn, e.g. \"npx\"."
+    },
+    "args": {
+      "type": "array",
+      "description": "stdio: arguments passed without shell interpolation.",
+      "items": {
+        "type": "string"
+      }
+    },
+    "env": {
+      "description": "stdio: extra environment variables as a string-to-string object."
+    },
+    "cwd": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "stdio: child working directory; omit to inherit."
+    },
+    "url": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "streamable-http: absolute http(s) MCP endpoint URL."
+    },
+    "headers": {
+      "description": "streamable-http: extra request headers as a string-to-string object."
+    },
+    "toolCallTimeoutMs": {
+      "type": "number",
+      "description": "Per-tool-call timeout in milliseconds; defaults to 60000."
+    }
+  },
+  "required": [
+    "name",
+    "transport"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/mcp/mcp-manager/src/tools.ts`](../packages/mcp/mcp-manager/src/tools.ts)
+
+### `mcp_manager_list`
+
+List the MCP servers configured for this harness with their transport, enabled state, connection status, and the tools each one currently contributes. Use it before adding or removing a server.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {}
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/mcp/mcp-manager/src/tools.ts`](../packages/mcp/mcp-manager/src/tools.ts)
+
+### `mcp_manager_remove`
+
+Remove a configured MCP server. Its tools stop being callable immediately and the stored entry is deleted.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "name": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Stable local namespace for this server (the model sees its tools as mcp__<name>__<tool>). Use [A-Za-z0-9_-], 1-32 characters; unique among configured servers."
+    }
+  },
+  "required": [
+    "name"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/mcp/mcp-manager/src/tools.ts`](../packages/mcp/mcp-manager/src/tools.ts)
+
+### `mcp_manager_set_enabled`
+
+Enable or disable a configured MCP server without deleting it. Disabling unmounts the client and removes its tools from the model view; enabling mounts it again.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "name": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Stable local namespace for this server (the model sees its tools as mcp__<name>__<tool>). Use [A-Za-z0-9_-], 1-32 characters; unique among configured servers."
+    },
+    "enabled": {
+      "type": "boolean",
+      "description": "True to mount the server, false to unmount it."
+    }
+  },
+  "required": [
+    "name",
+    "enabled"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/mcp/mcp-manager/src/tools.ts`](../packages/mcp/mcp-manager/src/tools.ts)
+
+The four management tools edit one persisted registry of external MCP servers; adding, removing, or disabling an entry mounts or disposes a child dsh-mcp-client, so the tools a server contributes appear and disappear with it. A deployment without a composed settings provider keeps the registry on the plugin config and the Web card reports itself unavailable.
