+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Model Experience
+
+### Management tools
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+Four small schemas: `mcp_manager_list`, `mcp_manager_add`, `mcp_manager_remove`, `mcp_manager_set_enabled`. Each returns pretty-printed JSON: the server list with transport, enabled state, connection status, target, tools, and configuration problems. Every management call changes which `mcp__<name>__*` tools are visible on the next request.
+
+#### Token effect
+
+Fixed schema cost on every request in that tool view, plus the cost of the MCP servers' own tool definitions — the reason servers are opt-in per entry.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+Adding, removing, or disabling a server changes the tool-definition prefix from the first changed schema token; an unchanged server set is prefix-stable.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- **The page shows configuration, not live connection health** — connection status is available through `mcp_manager_list`; the browser page renders only the stored registry.
+- **Credentials in `env` and `headers` are stored as plain settings values** — the section is not a secret store, so prefer credentials your shell already exports and reference them by name where the server supports it.
+- **Invalid entries are stored, not refused at write time** — schema-valid but unusable entries (an empty command, a non-HTTP URL) are skipped by reconciliation and reported in `problems`.
+- **`dsh-mcp-client` bridges tools only** — MCP resources and prompts remain unsupported.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+### Dev Note
+
+<details>
+<summary>Working context for maintainers — click to expand</summary>
+
+This Dev Note is working context for maintainers and explicitly non-authoritative — shipped behavior and limits live in the sections above and in the package code.
+
+- **The page was verified in a live browser, not only in jsdom** — adding the stdio fixture server from the add dialog spawned the child MCP process and wrote the `mcp-manager` settings section, the filter and the pager narrowed the list, disabling the server disposed the process, and deleting it returned the section to `[]`.
+- **The four management tools are catalogued** — they are registered in `docs/tool-catalog.md` and its Chinese mirror, so an edit to a tool description changes a generated document; keep angle-bracket placeholders inside backticks, because a bare `mcp__<name>__<tool>` fails the documentation-site build.
+
+</details>
